  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical ball $A$ of mass 4 kg, moving along a straight line strikes another spherical ball $B$ of mass $1 \\mathrm{kg}$ at rest. After the collision, $A$ and $B$ move with velocities $y_{1} \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}$ and $v_{2} \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}$ respectively making angles of $30^{\\circ}$ and $60^{\\circ}$ with\r\nrespect to the original direction of motion of $A .$ The ratio $\\frac{y_{1}}{v_{2}}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "yGaAK",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "R4nNf",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FNGQn",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IxaYX",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2012_phy_a23.png\">\r\n\r\nAlong $y$ -axis momentum remains zero. Here\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n4 v_{1} \\sin 30^{\\circ} &=v_{2} \\sin 60^{\\circ} \\\\\r\n\\frac{y_{1}}{v_{2}} &=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
